{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `W_z1`, `Y_z1_w1`, `Y_z1_w0`, and `Y_z0_w0`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the disallowed manual `target +=` likelihood with vectorized built-in Bernoulli sampling statements over deterministic top-level partitions of the originally scored data. `W_z1` is `W[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1`; `Y_z1_w1` is `Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1 && W[n] == 1`; `Y_z1_w0` is `Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1 && W[n] == 0`; and `Y_z0_w0` is `Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 0 && W[n] == 0`, all in original row order. The count variables are the corresponding lengths. For the `Z == 0, W == 0` branch, the Bernoulli mixture was collapsed using the identity `log_mix(pi_c, bernoulli_lpmf(y | eta_c0), bernoulli_lpmf(y | eta_n)) = bernoulli_lpmf(y | pi_c * eta_c0 + (1 - pi_c) * eta_n)` for binary `y`. Added the explicit density-neutral prior `pi_c ~ uniform(0, 1)` for the already bounded parameter `pi_c`. No new observation values were invented; the generated data are deterministic reshapes of the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N_z1;
  array[N_z1] int<lower=0, upper=1> W_z1;

  int<lower=0> N_z1_w1;
  array[N_z1_w1] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z1_w1;

  int<lower=0> N_z1_w0;
  array[N_z1_w0] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z1_w0;

  int<lower=0> N_z0_w0;
  array[N_z0_w0] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z0_w0;
}

parameters {
  // Population probability of being a complier
  real<lower=0, upper=1> pi_c;

  // Probabilities for the binomial outcome distributions
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_c0;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_c1;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_n;
}

model {
  // Prior for complier probability; density-neutral for the bounded parameter.
  pi_c ~ uniform(0, 1);

  // Priors for outcome model parameters
  eta_c0 ~ beta(2, 2);
  eta_c1 ~ beta(2, 2);
  eta_n ~ beta(2, 2);

  // Likelihood, expressed with SafeStan-compatible built-in distributions.
  W_z1 ~ bernoulli(pi_c);
  Y_z1_w1 ~ bernoulli(eta_c1);
  Y_z1_w0 ~ bernoulli(eta_n);
  Y_z0_w0 ~ bernoulli(pi_c * eta_c0 + (1 - pi_c) * eta_n);
}

generated quantities {
  // Superpopulation complier average causal effect (CACE)
  // in per-1000 units
  real CACE = (eta_c1 - eta_c0) * 10^3;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N_z1":0,"W_z1":[],"N_z1_w1":0,"Y_z1_w1":[],"N_z1_w0":0,"Y_z1_w0":[],"N_z0_w0":2,"Y_z0_w0":[1,0]}","protected_variables":["W_z1","Y_z1_w1","Y_z1_w0","Y_z0_w0"]}
